(177, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-230', 2289, 'Assessing Preferences and Feasibility of Multi-Seat Child Restraint Systems (CRS) for Multi-Child Households in Qatar', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 85, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:19', '2025-05-22 06:49:47', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', ' - Project\'s ID missing\n - Research Project Plan and Expected Outcomes (Not to exceed 3 pages)\n- in bugdet please specify the item needed in C and D (travel)\n - Travel policy: Only  awarded students are eligible for travel to a conference to present an accepted paper acknowledging grant support. \n - Any software requires ITS approval before purchase\n- please make sure that software and the book requested is not available or provide by QU\n - missing: Similarity Report (the similarity percentage should not exceed 10% excluding references and appendices) ', NULL, 7000, '7000 was spend for student attending his conference. The remaining 13000 has been committed to lease a software. The relevant forms have been submitted.', 'Mohamed Ahmed AlAwad, Mohamed Kharbeche, Faris Tarlochan. Assessing Preferences and Feasibility of Multi-Seat Child Restraint Systems (CRS) for Multi-Child Households in Qatar, Procedia Computer Science, Volume 257, 2025, Pages 495-502', 'Student was highly engaged', 'save', 0),
(178, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-244', 2290, 'Driver Behavior Analysis by Data Stratifications at Signalized vs. Non-Signalized Roundabouts in Doha', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 76, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:19', '2025-05-22 04:29:22', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', ' - please make sure that the book requested is not available or provide by QU\n - Travel policy: Only  awarded students are eligible for travel to a conference to present an accepted paper acknowledging grant support\n- tablets are not allowed\n- in Misc: fuel cost for 2 indiv. is not allowed\n- Tablets are not allowed please remove them from the budget\n- proposal not signed\n - Project\'s ID missing', NULL, 9147, 'Journal publication', '[Mohammed Abul Fahed, Pilsung Choe and Al-Harith Umlai], [Applied Sciences], [Q1, SCIE, Scopus indexed]', 'A student was involved in authoring the paper and collect and analyze the data', 'save', 0),
(179, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-248', 2291, 'Potential enhancements in Legislation to Promote Curbside Eating in Qatar: A Case Study of Lusail Food Street', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 86, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:20', '2025-09-03 03:20:28', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', '  - Project\'s ID missing\n - Research Project Plan and Expected Outcomes (Not to exceed 3 pages)\n- please make sure that the books requested is not available or provide by QU\n- please clarify sesri?\n- SESRI not for free?\n- missing similarity report', NULL, 0, 'None of the allocated budget for the project was spent due to delays experienced with the journal to which the research paper was submitted for publication. As a result, no publication-related costs have been incurred to date. Furthermore, no books or additional resources were purchased for the project, as all necessary materials were accessible either through the university library or via interlibrary lending services.', '[Sanitha Aboobacker  Abdul Jaleel 1,  Tarryn Nicole  Kennedy Paquet2  and Amina Al  Kandari3], [Curbside Eating in  Qatar: Regulatory  Challenges and  Adaptive  Governance  solutions in Lusail  Food Street ], Cities: The  Internation  al Journal  of Urban  Policy and  Planning', 'The student actively participated in all stages of the research on food trucks in Qatar, focusing on zoning, permitting, cultural norms, and regulatory barriers. She engaged with stakeholders and community members, speaking to people about the topic addressed to her and gathering valuable insights. As part of the project, she conducted both qualitative and quantitative data collection through interviews, surveys, and compiling responses related to the operational and regulatory challenges faced by food trucks. Additionally, she went through the entire QU-IRB process to obtain ethical clearance for the study. Based on the collected data, she contributed to writing a research paper, which has been completed and is currently in the publication process. Her dedication and involvement have significantly supported the successful progress and outcomes of the project.', 'save', 0),
(180, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-252', 2292, 'Development of a Portable Emission Reduction System.', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 80, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:20', '2025-05-29 02:33:59', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', ' - Wrong template has been used. Please use the template availabe in QU website: https://www.qu.edu.qa/en-us/research/offices/research-support/internal-grants/studentgrant \n - Project\'s ID missing\n - student signatures missing\n - missing: Similarity Report (the similarity percentage should not exceed 10% excluding references and appendices) ', NULL, 9990, 'Manufacturing of the test section - Setting up the test rig- Purchasing of fuel injection system - Purchasing of Monoethanolamine chemical for the experiments', 'None', 'Designing an emission reduction system that can lower pollutants such as CO2, NOx, \r\nand smoke from diesel engine exhaust gases is the goal of this project. All the students have engaged in producing an efficient design and building the test rig. The first step in the procedure \r\nis to identify the issue of emissions from diesel engine trucks, such as CO2, NOx, and smoke. \r\nThis is followed by a thorough investigation and gathering of data. Developing and testing \r\nstrategies to safely capture and store these pollutants is the next stage. The prototype was \r\nconstructed, tested, and improved depending on input from prospective customers when the \r\nmost effective approach has been identified. Following these procedures, the efficiency of the prototype has been verified.', 'save', 0),
(181, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-255', 2293, 'Optimizing Sustainability performance of building structures: Use of Generative Design in BIM', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 77, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:22', '2025-05-17 12:04:22', b'0', '20,000', 'Awarded', ' - Project\'s ID missing\n - Please clarify why this project is not linked to a course\n- clarify the status of pending approval\n-  - Travel policy: Only  awarded students are eligible for travel to a conference to present an accepted paper acknowledging grant support. ', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
(182, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-257', 2294, 'Computer Vision-Based Smart Home Care System for Alzheimer’s Patients', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 81, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:23', '2025-05-26 01:43:09', b'0', '9560', 'Awarded', NULL, NULL, 0, 'The students undertook the project as part of their SDP, which spanned two semesters (SDP1 and SDP2). By the end of the first semester, they had initiated the hardware implementation. Since the project funds were only released at the start of the second semester, and to prevent delays in progress, we utilized existing hardware components from previous projects and departmental resources. As a result, the allocated budget for this project was not used.', '', 'The students successfully developed an innovative vision-based smart home care system to be designed to enhance the safety and well-being of Alzheimer\'s patients by providing real-time notifications to caregivers, helping to prevent accidents like falls and wandering. The system integrates live tracking technology, computer vision-based fall detection, and an IoT-enabled caregiver interface to provide continuous monitoring and support.\r\nEach student submitted four individual progress reports, along with two final group reports. Additionally, they delivered two presentations—one at the end of each semester.\r\nTwo of the students received B+ grades, while one student earned an A.', 'save', 0),
(183, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-258', 2295, 'Enhancing Home Care: A Smart Wearable Solution for Alzheimer\'s Patients', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 81, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:28', '2025-05-26 01:44:19', b'0', '8100', 'Awarded', NULL, NULL, 0, 'The students undertook the project as part of their SDP, which spanned two semesters (SDP1 and SDP2). By the end of the first semester, they had initiated the hardware implementation. Since the project funds were only released at the start of the second semester, and to prevent delays in progress, we utilized existing hardware components from previous projects and departmental resources. As a result, the allocated budget for this project was not used.', '', 'The students successfully developed a system that provides an effective and reliable solution for remote monitoring of patients, specifically tailored for individuals with Alzheimer’s disease. The system combines a wearable device, a cloud-based processing unit, and a mobile application to enable continuous monitoring, real-time event detection, and timely alerts for caregivers.\r\nEach student submitted four individual progress reports, along with two final group reports. Additionally, they delivered two presentations—one at the end of each semester.\r\nAll students achieved an A grade and are currently in the process of preparing a journal paper.', 'save', 0),
(184, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-263', 2296, 'Simultaneous Localization and Mapping Mobile Robot', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 82, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:30', '2025-05-27 08:08:56', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', ' - proposal not signed\n- please note that the total budget should not exceed 10,000 QR', NULL, 6183, 'Items Purchased:\r\nLidar Sensor\r\nRobot Platform\r\nVision Module\r\nDepth Sensor', '-', 'The project was divided into 2 main subsystems, 1. Robot Vision and SLAM Algorition, 2. Robot Locomotion. \r\n\r\nThe students went through engagemnet sessions to accomplish the project objectives.  Students were provided guide and supervision in achieving the objectives.  Following are the task accomplished by the students. \r\n\r\nVision System (Atheer Robelah)  \r\n1.	Developed an Accurate SLAM Algorithm: Refine a SLAM algorithm that combines visual and LiDAR data to achieve precise real-time mapping and localization, ensuring adaptability across diverse scenarios.\r\n2.	Designed an Effective Navigation System with Integrated Sensors and Actuators: Develop a navigation system that integrates visual and LiDAR sensors with actuators for effective obstacle detection and avoidance. This system enables real-time processing and data fusion to support rapid movement while evaluating overall performance.\r\n3.	Developed and Implemented Techniques for Character and Number Processing: Develop processing methods focused on number and character identification to enable the robot to determine locations.\r\n\r\n\r\n Robot Locomotion (Noora Saker). \r\n1.	DesignED a Wheeled Mobile Robot: DesignED and constructed a wheeled mobile robot with a robust chassis that enables flexible, agile, and rapid movement, utilizing wheel configurations that enhance maneuverability and ensure accurate orientation control.\r\n2.	Integrated SLAM with Character and Number Recognition: Incorporated the SLAM system and character and number recognition into the robot, ensuring smooth operation to enhance navigation, obstacle detection, and localization.', 'save', 0),
(185, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-264', 2297, 'Deep Learning Frameworks for Automated Detection and Grading of Cancers from Histopathological Images', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 78, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:31', '2025-09-04 06:18:31', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', ' - Please clarify why this project is not linked to a course\n - please note that 10,000 is the maximum amount for undergrad projects, please adjust your budget accordingly\n- please attach similarity report', NULL, 0, NULL, 'Hissa Al-Kuwari, Belqes Alshami, Muhammad Arsalan, Aisha Al-Khinji, Hassan Rizvi, \"Automated Detection and Grading of Renal Cell Carcinoma in Histopathological Images via Efficient Attention Transformer Network\", Diagnostics', 'Data curation, data Augmentation, Experiment Using deep learning, writing the first draft of the paper', 'save', 0),
(186, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-269', 2298, 'Evaluating Project Delivery Methods for Green Building Development: Insights from Industry Professionals in Qatar', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 77, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:32', '2025-05-17 12:04:32', b'0', '20,000', 'Awarded', ' - Project\'s ID missing\n - Please clarify why this project is not linked to a course\n- clarify the status of pending approval\n - Travel policy: Only  awarded students are eligible for travel to a conference to present an accepted paper acknowledging grant support. \n- enrollment letter should be for spring 2025', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
(187, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-274', 2299, 'Integrated Additive Manufacturing and CNC Machine', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 82, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:33', '2025-05-27 08:18:49', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', NULL, NULL, 4287, 'Items purchased\r\n- Laser range sensor\r\n- Vision Module\r\n- Jetson nano', '-', 'Students went throught the following engagement sessions;\r\n1. Additive manufacturing process: The students were introduced to the 3D printings and other types of additive manufacturing available in the market. \r\n2. CNC Machining: Students were introduced to material removal processes including laser and mechanical removal. \r\n3. Student were introduced to G: Code and Fusion 360 softwares. \r\n\r\nThe following items were accomplished by the students;\r\n\r\n1.	Design of hybrid 3D printing system: Developed a comprehensive design for the hybrid 3D printer and CNC machine, detailing dimensions, materials, and components required.\r\n2.	Development of the machine: Identified and sourced all necessary mechanical and electronic components and proceed with the construction and assembly of the machine according to design specifications.\r\n3.	Development of algorithms:	Programed and integrated control systems to enable the operation of both 3D printing and CNC functionalities.\r\n\r\nStudents demonstrated a good progress towards completing the project.', 'save', 0),
