(189, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-279', 2301, 'Smart Glasses for Real-Time Navigation and Obstacle Avoidance for Visually Impaired Users', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 83, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:37', '2025-05-27 07:53:05', b'0', '9075', 'Awarded', NULL, NULL, 4448, 'Bought the following equipment:\r\n- Raspberry Pi microcontroller.\r\n- Raspberry Pi cameras.\r\n- Ultrasonic Sensors.\r\n- Inertial Measurement Unit (IMU).\r\n- 3D design and printing.\r\n- 4G Module.\r\n- Customs duty\r\n- Customs Duty and Admin fees.', '', 'The students were involved in:\r\n1) Specifying functional requirements and design constraints for the product.\r\n2) Designing the full system including hardware, software and Communication modules.\r\n3) Implementing the designed system and integrating all modules.\r\n4) Testing and evaluating the implemented system against the functional requirements and design constraints.\r\n5) Writing a report for the senior design project course.\r\n6) Presenting and showcasing a demo for the project.', 'save', 0),
(190, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-282', 2302, 'Brain Controlled Prosthetic Arm', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 83, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:40', '2025-05-27 07:44:35', b'0', '9330', 'Awarded', ' - Any software requires ITS approval before purchase\n- please make sure that software and the book requested is not available or provide by QU', NULL, 3059, 'Bought the following equipment:\r\n- Insight 5 channels wireless EEG headset.\r\n- Seromotors\r\n- Micro SD cards\r\n- Batteries.\r\n- Customs Duty and Admin fees.', '', 'The students were involved in:\r\n1) Specifying functional requirements and design constraints for the product.\r\n2) Designing the full system including hardware, software and Communication modules.\r\n3) Implementing the designed system and integrating all modules.\r\n4) Testing and evaluating the implemented system against the functional requirements and design constraints.\r\n5) Writing a report for the senior design project course.\r\n6) Presenting and showcasing a demo for the project.', 'save', 0),
(191, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-284', 2303, 'Study on PSF/PVP Blend Membrane for CO2/N2 Separation', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 89, 45, '2025-05-17 12:04:42', '2026-04-30 04:46:14', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', ' - Project\'s ID missing (please do not change the original template)', NULL, 19740, 'Chemicals which are 1-Butyl-3-methylimidazolium tetrafluoroborate, Polysulfone, Polyvinylpyrrolidone, and 1-Methyl-2-pyrrolidinone ReagentPlus', 'Polysulfone-PolyVinyl Pyrrolidone Blend Membrane for CO2/N2 Separation. In Re-Submission process.', 'The student was actively involved in conducting a comprehensive literature review and developing the experimental procedure for the preparation of membranes for gas separation. This work included critically analyzing recent studies to identify suitable materials, fabrication techniques, and performance benchmarks for efficient gas separation.\r\n\r\nHe contributed to the selection of appropriate polymer matrices and additives, aiming to enhance membrane selectivity and permeability. In addition, he participated in optimizing the membrane fabrication process by adjusting key parameters such as composition, solvent choice, casting conditions, and post-treatment methods. These efforts were directed toward achieving high-performance membranes with improved stability and separation efficiency.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, he was engaged in evaluating membrane performance based on gas separation criteria, ensuring that the prepared membranes met the desired specifications for selectivity, permeability, and overall operational reliability.', 'save', 0),
