(219, 'QUST-1-CENG-2025-377', 2331, 'AI-Powered Learning and Signal Analysis for Valvular Heart Disease Detection: A Hands-On Approach Using Digital Stethoscope and Audio Signal Processing', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 16, 45, '2025-05-17 12:05:16', '2025-06-02 16:20:07', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', ' - Project\'s ID missing\n- Abdulla\'s enrollment letter should be for spring 2025\n- explain the need of Stethoscope with accessories and misc requisted? and why you cannot use the provided tools in labs?\n- the equipment in misc should be moved to materials if justified', NULL, 0, 'We were informed that ITS approval is required for the purchase of project equipment. Unfortunately, we did not receive updates on the approval. Therefore, we could not use the budget and could not acquire any real-time data.', '', 'Both students actively participated and learnt new knowledge. They designed and developed signal filtering, feature extraction, feature selection and supervised machine learning to classify normal and abnormal heart sounds. Publicly available data was used because we could not purchase equipment. The students developed a graphical user interface to load, visualize and classify signals.', 'save', 0),
