(316, 'QUST-2-CAS-2025-439', 2373, 'Molecular and Bioinformatics Analysis of the SPL Gene Family in Native Date Palm (Phoenix dactylifera', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 130, 52, '2026-04-04 13:34:38', '2026-04-22 06:36:08', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', ' - Project ID is missing\n- please mention the linked course\'s name and number\n- please re-upload your proposal attaching the similarity report and student signature', 'Awarded', 8146, 'to buy a plant miRNA purification kit and miRNA-specific primers for  date palm', 'Noor Al-Hilali, Genome-Wide Identification and Analysis of SPL genes in date palm (Phoenix dactylifera), Bachlor thesis, Department of Biological and Environmental Sciences, Qatar University, Doha, Qatar', 'Noor Al Hilali was engaged in all research activities of the project titled \"Genome-Wide Identification and Analysis of SPL Genes in Date Palm (Phoenix dactylifera)\" under my supervision. The project is part of the Student Grant Application for the 2025 Cycle 1 and is linked to the course BIOL497. \r\nNoor\'s research focuses on bioinformatics work to identify and characterize the SPL gene family in date palms, with particular emphasis on miRNA-regulated genes.\r\nThe project involves several tasks, including identifying the SPL gene family, performing sequence analysis, and conducting phylogenetic analysis. Noor has completed the identification of the SPL gene family and is currently working on OMICS analyses and manuscript preparation. The research aims to investigate the role of SPL genes in plant growth and development, particularly in response to environmental stressors.\r\nThe project provided valuable insights into the SPL transcription factor family and its role in plant adaptation and yield characteristics. \r\nNoor gained training skills in bioinformatics and research design, which will contribute to her academic and professional development.\r\n\r\nProgress Overview:\r\n-Noor successfully identified the SPL gene family in date palm by analyzing DNA, RNA, and protein sequences from various databases. This task was completed within the expected timeframe of September to October 2025.\r\n\r\n-She conducted a thorough analysis of the sequences, defining specific variants and their effects on transcription and translation. This analysis was completed in November 2025.\r\n\r\n-She identified conserved motifs, miRNA-binding sites, domain predictions, and intron-exon distributions. This task was completed by December 2025.\r\n\r\n-Noor performed a phylogenetic analysis of the SPL gene family, defining specific clusters among SPL genes based on their sequences. This analysis was completed in January 2026.\r\n\r\n-She completed OMICS analyses, including genomic, transcriptome, and protein analysis. Noor has successfully submitted her bachelor\'s thesis, which encompasses all the tasks and findings from her research project.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, Noor Al Hilali has demonstrated exceptional dedication and skill in completing all assigned tasks for her research project. Her work has significantly contributed to the understanding of SPL genes in date palms, and her upcoming manuscript will further disseminate these findings to the scientific community.\r\nNoor graduated in fall 2025 and is currently preparing a manuscript for publication in a journal, which is expected to be completed by the end of this semester.', 'save', 0),
(317, 'QUST-2-CAS-2025-442', 2374, 'Exploration of the soil beneficial bacterial diversity and related natural products from Qatar’s environment\nrelated natural products from Qatar’s environment', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 190, 52, '2026-04-04 13:34:41', '2026-04-14 09:16:32', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', ' - please correct project\'s ID\n- similarity report missing', 'Awarded', 0, 'the allocated budget was not utilized as we already had sufficient consumables available in the laboratory to carry out the planned activities. Therefore, no additional purchases were necessary during the project period.\nKindly, as a suggestion for future consideration, it may be helpful to allow a longer period (e.g., more than three months, September–November) for utilizing student grant funds, as additional time is often required to obtain quotations and complete the procurement process.', 'QULSS Nov. 2025. Oral and Poster : Title: Decoding Microbial Interactions: From Soil Metagenome to Biotechnological Applications', 'N/A', 'save', 0),
