(319, 'QUST-2-CAS-2025-445', 2376, 'Development of Novel Catalysts: Efficient Hybrid LDHs- MOFs and LDHs-Biochar Composites', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 191, 52, '2026-04-04 13:34:49', '2026-04-27 08:14:24', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', 'None', 'Awarded', 18744, 'Purchase of CM-26A UV LAMP: Length: 12 in (30 cm) 12 in (30 cm); Width: 9 in (22.8 cm) 9 in (22.8 cm) Height: 6.5 in (16.5 cm) 6.5 in (16.5 cm) Light Source: ENF-240C Lamp Style: Handheld UV Lamp\" for monitoring of photocatalysis equilibrium and kinetics.\r\nChemicals and solvents for synthesis of LDHs and MOFs', 'M.Sc. Thesis in Materials Sciences - Presented December 2025', 'The M.Sc. student - Ms. Ranim Al-Soufi was comprehensively engaged in all stages of the project, demonstrating independence, technical expertise, and scholarly commitment. She successfully executed the entire practical component, which encompassed the synthesis of biochar, layered double hydroxides (LDHs), metal–organic frameworks (MOFs), and their composite materials, and then testing the synthesized materials for integrated adsorption-photocatalysis. Her responsibilities included experimental design, optimization of synthesis conditions, laboratory execution, systematic data collection, and advanced analytical characterization. She applied a wide range of techniques, FTIR, XRD, BET surface area analysis, SEM/TEM imaging, and adsorption-photocatalysis studies, to evaluate the structural, morphological, and functional properties of the synthesized materials against a variety of organic pollutants in individual and mixture matrices.\r\nBeyond the experimental phase, she prepared the complete written documentation, including thesis drafting, refinement of the manuscript, and preparation of supporting materials. She also managed the oral presentation and defense of her thesis, responded thoroughly to examiners’ and reviewers’ comments, and carried out all required thesis corrections. Furthermore, she contributed significantly to the preparation of manuscripts for both a review article and a research paper, ensuring the dissemination of the project’s findings to the wider scientific community.\r\nHer comprehensive involvement, from material synthesis and characterization to academic writing, peer review responses, thesis corrections, and manuscript preparation for publication, demonstrates her research capabilities.', 'save', 0),
