(341, 'QUST-2-CENG-2025-464', 2398, 'Investigation of Oxytetracycline Removal using Mixed Matrix Membranes', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 89, 52, '2026-04-04 13:35:08', '2026-04-30 04:40:00', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', 'None', 'Awarded', 9575, 'Chemicals which are 3-Aminopropyl)trimethoxysilane, B - C y c l o d e x t r i n, Poly(ethylene glycol) diacrylate, Chloroform', 'The manuscript in progress to be submitted to a journal.', 'Students were actively involved in preparing the literature review and developing the experimental procedures for membrane fabrication used in gas separation applications. They conducted an in-depth review of relevant scientific publications to understand current advancements, materials, and methodologies, and then translated this knowledge into a structured experimental plan. This included selecting appropriate materials, defining preparation steps, and outlining testing protocols to evaluate membrane performance.', 'save', 0),
