(349, 'QUST-2-CENG-2025-521', 2406, 'Deep Learning-Based Smart Framework for Corrosion Detection and Prognosis in Infrastructure', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 210, 52, '2026-04-04 13:35:18', '2026-04-16 04:49:26', b'0', '19000', NULL, '* please note that travel is allowed for students only\n - project\'s ID is missing\n- please re-attach student ID and the similarity report and re-upload the proposal to the system', 'Awarded', 11877, 'Participation in the Net-Zero Future Conference 2025, Cape Town, South Africa, 5 – 7 November 2025:\r\nDiem at 1500 QAR per day for 3 days: 4500 QAR\r\nVisa application fee: 130 QAR\r\nAir tickets: 5570 QAR\r\nConference fee (400 EURO): 1677 QAR\r\nTotal spending: 11877 QAR', '(1) Mati Ullah, Vagelis Plevris, and Afaq Ahmad, “Towards Efficient Corrosion Monitoring: A Comparative Study of Modern YOLO and R-CNN Architectures”, Net-Zero Future Conference 2025, Cape Town, South Africa, 5 – 7 November 2025. (2) Mati Ullah and Vagelis Plevris, “Deep Learning-Based Smart Framework for Corrosion Detection Using CNN and Transformer Architectures”, ARTISTE 2025 – The First International Conference on Artificial Intelligence in Structural Engineering, Torino, Italy, September 14–17, 2025.', 'The student actively contributed to the preparation, implementation, and dissemination of research outcomes under the project “Deep Learn-ing-Based Smart Framework for Corrosion Detection and Prognosis in Infrastructure”. The student developed deep learning models for corrosion detection and segmentation, including YOLO, R-CNN, CNN, and transformer-based architectures. The student also prepared datasets, performed annotation, training, hyperparameter tuning, and evaluation of the models. Research findings were disseminated through conference publications and presentations at international conferences, contributing to the visibility of the project and enhancing the student’s research, technical, and academic communication skills.', 'save', 0),
