(361, 'QUST-2-CHS-2025-449', 2418, 'Feasibility Study of a Two-Week Living Lab for Profiling Student Lifestyles ', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 216, 52, '2026-04-04 13:35:31', '2026-04-04 13:35:31', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', 'Raghad Elashie has expired QUID\n- could you please clarify the need of printing fees, while QU printers are available', 'Awarded', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
(362, 'QUST-2-CHS-2025-452', 2419, 'Functional assessment of KCNA10 gene using zebrafish model', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 217, 52, '2026-04-04 13:35:33', '2026-04-20 07:57:13', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', '* Maryam Abdulfattah Shafie QUID is not provided\n* Please add Plagiarism report with percentage not exceeding 10%\n- project ID is missing\n- please move publication fees under section C in budget\n- LPI\'s and student\'s signatures are missing\n', 'Awarded', 10000, 'Morphoinos for the knoecdown experiments', 'under prep', 'Morpholino-mediated knockdown of zebrafish ackr3a and ackr3b has been successfully established, with titration experiments identifying 0.75 mM as the optimal concentration for effective gene suppression with minimal toxicity. Preliminary phenotypic assessment demonstrates dose-dependent cardiac abnormalities, including reduced heart rate and impaired blood flow during early embryonic development. Rescue experiments using in vitro transcribed human ACKR3wild-type mRNA show promising results, with restoration of cardiac function toward control levels, supporting the specificity of the observed phenotype. In parallel, variant validation using Sanger sequencing is underway to confirm findings from initial genomic analyses. Overall, these results indicate steady progress in characterizing the functional role of ACKR3 in cardiovascular development.', 'save', 0),
(363, 'QUST-2-CHS-2025-461', 2420, 'Exploring the Anti-Proliferative Activities of Engineered Antimicrobial Peptides in Breast Cancer Cells  ', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 218, 52, '2026-04-04 13:35:34', '2026-04-13 04:27:27', b'0', '10000', 'Awarded', 'Please correct the total budget: put coma instead of the dot', 'Awarded', 9281, '1. Annexin V-FITC/PI Apoptosis kit (E-CK-A211) 200\r\n2. Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH) Cytotoxicity Color\r\n3. AlamarBlue™ Cell Viability Reagent. 100 mLrimetric Assay Kit 96T\r\n3.', 'NA', 'The project “Exploring the Anti-Proliferative Activities of Engineered Antimicrobial Peptides in Breast Cancer Cells” has actively engaged students Falwa Rashid, H. S. Naheyan, Noora Abdulla, and I. H. Ibrahim in both experimental and computational components of biomedical research. The students participated extensively in laboratory activities, including mammalian cell culture techniques, maintenance of breast cancer cell lines, and the execution of cell viability assays to evaluate the anti-proliferative effects of engineered peptides. They gained hands-on experience in assay preparation, data acquisition, and interpretation of results. In parallel, the students demonstrated strong commitment to developing competencies in bioinformatics, particularly in the use of computational tools for the design and optimization of anticancer peptides. This integrated training approach has strengthened their understanding of translational research, bridging in silico peptide design with in vitro biological validation', 'save', 0),
(364, 'QUST-2-CHS-2025-486', 2421, 'Elucidating the Role of STAT Signaling in T-Cell Response in Severe ICU cases of SARS COVID-19 Viral Infections and Sepsis', 'Accepted', NULL, NULL, '0.00', 117, 52, '2026-04-04 13:35:35', '2026-04-04 13:35:35', b'0', '20000', 'Awarded', ' - project ID is missing', 'Awarded', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
